<title>USA: Kansas fed cattle trade at standstill - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas fed cattle trade at standstill - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales of slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry was moderate and demand light. Last sales Monday were $65.00, wiht a few bids $64.00-$65.00. Asking prices were $66.00-$67.00. For the week to date, sales were confirmed on 5,000 head of mostly formula and contract cattle.</p>
<p>Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink. Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
